BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Liz and the Blue Bird: Asian Heritage Month Film Screening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T170000
UID:69d80132e2a2952aed0dbb4a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:May is Asian Heritage Month. Join us for a screening of\nLiz a
 nd the Blue Bird\n(2018)\n. This film's language is Japanese with English
  subtitles.\n"Mizore is shy and soft-spoken\, while her best friend Nozomi
  is outgoing. The two girls grow closer as they practice for their last du
 et before graduating high school. However\, the impending separation may b
 e more than their friendship can handle. Interspersed with their story is 
 the fantasy tale of Liz\, who like Mizore\, seeks a friendship that may be
  too hard to hold onto in this beautiful coming-of-age story."\nDrop in.
LOCATION:Dufferin/St.Clair\, Earlscourt Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d80132e2a2952aed0dbb4a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Loops\, Swoops and Curlicues Exhibition Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260505T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260505T153000
UID:6967f4954a9fd98b7f779e58@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How well can you read handwritten items? This free guided tour
  of\nLoops\, Swoops and Curlicues: A legacy of handwritten history\nwill l
 ead your through hundreds of years of handwritten items from TPL Special C
 ollections.\nCome test your decoding skills as we explore several hundred 
 years of handwritten words.\nRegistration is encouraged\, but not required
 . There is space for drop-in guests. Please meet at the entrance to the TD
  Gallery.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on thi
 s form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librari
 es Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be 
 used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questio
 ns about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answe
 rline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, To
 ronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, TD Gallery\, First Floor of Toronto R
 eference Library
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6967f4954a9fd98b7f779e58
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Indigenous Film Screening - Nechako: It Will Be a Big River Again
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T193000
UID:69c29efebf48d63c596c9a1e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Nechako\nis a crucial documentary from Lyana Patrick that foll
 ows two Indigenous Nations fighting for our collective future. When the Ke
 nney Dam was built in the 1950s\, it diverted 70 percent of the Nechako Ri
 ver into an artificial reservoir\, severely impacting the lives of local S
 tellat’en and Saik’uz Nations. What followed were decades of resistanc
 e\, including legal actions against the Canadian federal and provincial go
 vernments and Rio Tinto Alcan\, a subsidiary of a global mining conglomera
 te.\nNechako\nfollows the people fighting today to restore a river and a w
 ay of life: Nations going up against industry\, community leaders advocati
 ng for their people\, Elders documenting their histories and community mem
 bers living off the land. An urgent call to action\, Patrick’s film asks
  what survival looks like when it serves everyone\, in a story 70 years in
  the making—a story of hope and resistance against all odds\, amidst lar
 ge-scale environmental destruction and despite the will of powerful instit
 utions.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this 
 form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries
  Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be us
 ed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions
  about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerl
 ine staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toro
 nto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c29efebf48d63c596c9a1e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
